efore the starvation promotion (SGLANG_AX_DEADLINE_MAX_WAIT_S 120->600, warm stays 120; user: lost giants must not displace rescuable heads) + native in-batch prefix hold only for shared prefixes >= 4096 tokens (IN_BATCH_PREFIX_CACHING_DEPRIORITIZE_THRESHOLD 32->4096; Codex: the 35k/56k heads in ezn8 and the 19k head in ezm8 were held by a same-pack giant over a 413-token prefix and fell behind it) (chain-first check: at N26 the pin moved a 222k head ahead of a 35k and a 56k head in the opening, +2 chain misses) (Codex codex/fix-chainmax-0927: 131 rank0-broadcast cadence + auto chunk + in-flight cost; 132 report and 124 guard) + KDA state pool pinned at 400 slots (single change vs ezn3; without MTP the engine auto-sizes it to 779 slots = 13.4 GB per GPU while peak use was ~110 slots, and the KV pool shrank 1.37M -> 1.26M; expected pool ~1.8M, no KV wall) (user: spend fast/TPOT margin, protect chain starts). S6 base (S1 settings, no DCP, running 32,
